      "body": "# PR type\n- [x] Bug Fix\n- [ ] New Feature\n- [ ] Document Updates\n- [ ] More Models or Datasets Support\n\n# PR information\nFixes #10429\n\nWhen encoding multi-turn samples whose generated assistant token sequences do not already contain the non-thinking response prefix, `replace_assistant_response_with_ids` previously restored that prefix only for the final assistant turn. Earlier turns consequently lacked the template prefix in the training input.\n\nApply the supplied response prefix independently to every generated assistant turn and assign zero loss to inserted prefix tokens. Preserve an already present, zero-masked prefix and keep sampled token values and their loss masks intact.\n\nThis change uses the sample-level prefix supplied by the training encoder. It does not introduce per-turn template metadata or support for changing the response prefix between turns.\n\n## Experiment results\nValidated the exact two-file change from `local/fix/10429` at `92a6b4f422c7551a2ba4f73c5ee154a7baf2e5fe`, against main `680df5c670d7e8add906ac49381d603869410612`. The replacement commit preserves the same source tree.\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest -q tests/utils/test_multi_turn_response_prefix.py\n# 3 passed, 1 warning\npre-commit run --all-files\n# All 10 configured hooks passed\n```\n\nThe CPU tests exercise the production helper for multiple assistant turns, an existing masked prefix, and sampled prefix-token values. They do not constitute an end-to-end training, real-tokenizer, or accelerator validation. The author also reports prior validation; no additional quantitative claim is made without its execution record.\n\n# Checklist\n- [x] I have linked the related issue above, if there is one.\n- [ ] I have reviewed and understand every changed line, and I can explain how the change works and why it is correct.\n- [x] I have run the relevant tests or reproductions locally, and included the commands and results above (if applicable).\n- [ ] I am responsible for the content of this PR, regardless of how it was produced.\n\n## AI assistance\nOpenAI Codex assisted with inspection, CPU regression tests, formatting checks, and this author-requested update of the existing pull request. Human review and responsibility remain with the author.\n",
